if you want store post message in memory without db, if this message only available one time for a long chain function call
like A call B, but B is a post may stuck, it require a few time, message only available in this function call chain, use instance attribute
can share variables to avoid like B=C(); A(B)

class Service:
    def __init__(self):
        self.msg = []

    def call(self, request):
        self.request = request
        self.new_msg = change(request)
        self.post()
        self.next()

    def post():
        do(self.new_msg, self.request)

    def chat(self, request):
        self.msg.append(request)


@app.post("/api/run")
async def f(request: str = Form()):
    service = Service()
    service.call(request)


if you want the next post can use the previous post message like chat

service = Service()
@app.post("/api/chat")
async def chat(request: str = Form()):
    service.chat(request)

since Service is initialized outside of function chat, so it can store message per request
also you can store msg in data class

class Service:
    msg: list
    @staticmethod
    def chat(cls, request):
        cls.msg.append(request)
